zations in certain circles there's  a particular loathing for what's termed  biased news and a belief in the option  of a decent news organization which is  going to always an inherently be  unbiased unfortunately there is simply  no way of providing and factual unbiased  answers to the really big issues facing  society's news organizations that boast  about their neutrality forget that  neutrality is simply impossible visa vie  they're really urgent questions  confronting our civilization the word  bias ultimately simply alludes to the  business of having a tank on existence  one may have a better or worse take but  one needs attained  one needs eventually to tackle the  question of what's important just and  worth striving for if news or  information or even philosophy are going  to matter to us really matter they will  have to be presented to us by  organizations that have tried to think  through the ends of human life that have  a vision of where we're trying to go as  a species and that if somewhere  articulated their answers to their  audiences the issue is not there for the  illusory and timid one between bias and  fact but between better and worse  varieties of bias we should never knock  to take the most obvious examples  America's Fox News or Britain's Daily  Mail just on the basis that they are  biased we should only ever argue that  they seem badly biased that's the battle  to fight we also need an extension of  our sense of what sort of bias can exist  at present we're used to thinking of  bias simply in terms of right and left  but this is a radical reduction in the  kinds of bias that are theoretically  available to us we don't always have to  limit things to a choice between blue  and red we might discover a bias in  favor of the wisdom of more tamely the  dark consoling pessimism of Schopenhauer  or the wit and humanity of Marcel Proust  we could be biased towards ambiguity  cheerful despair or insane insanity our  societies would be richer if we were  better not as stripping facts of bias  but at developing our capacities for  higher bias all individuals and  organizations even ones like the BBC  Wikipedia or a great university in fact  believe in all sorts of things deep down  they aren't as neutral as they want us  to think  that is an extremely good thing so it's  high time for them to stop hiding behind  a false defense of their factual  impartiality and to come out from behind  the shadows with a clear articulation of  their vision of a good society it's time  for biases to conflict openly as part of  a healthy democratic process we don't  need our information stripped of bias we  need to evolve our way through clash of  ideologies towards the best kinds of  bias furthermore we'll have matured when  we start to know where our own biases  really are and so start to get less  prickly and touchy about the biases of  others thank you for watching remember  to like the video and subscribe to our  channel for more  you
 

